{title:Title}

{p 8 17 2}
{bf:stataedu} -- Stata beginner's learning program: installation and basics

{title:Syntax}

{p 8 13 2}
{cmd:stataedu} [{cmd:install} {cmd:basic} {cmd:example} {cmd:all}]

{title:Description}

{p 4 4 2}
{cmd:stataedu} is an entry-level learning program for Stata beginners,
published by Dingyuan Accounting, which follows the academic principle of
{bf:scientific and standardized, humane and good}. In three short lessons
it helps you get to know Stata quickly: installing the software, the
interface and the most frequently used commands, and a complete worked
example.

{p 4 4 2}
With no options, {cmd:stataedu} displays all three lessons in turn. Use the
options to review a single lesson at any time.

{title:Options}

{p 4 4 2}
{cmd:install} displays only lesson 1: how to download, install, and activate Stata (about 10 minutes).

{p 4 4 2}
{cmd:basic} displays only lesson 2: the five areas of the Stata interface and the 10 most frequently used commands.

{p 4 4 2}
{cmd:example} displays only lesson 3: a complete, ready-to-run worked example.

{p 4 4 2}
{cmd:all} displays all three lessons (the default).

{title:Examples}

{p 4 4 2}
{cmd:. stataedu}

{p 4 4 2}
Displays all three lessons.

{p 4 4 2}
{cmd:. stataedu, install}

{p 4 4 2}
Displays only the installation steps.

{p 4 4 2}
{cmd:. stataedu, basic example}

{p 4 4 2}
Displays the basics and the worked example together.

{title:Remarks}

{p 4 4 2}
{bf:Learning tips}

{p 4 8 2}
1. Run {cmd:stataedu} and read all three lessons first.

{p 4 8 2}
2. Open the Do-file editor (Ctrl+9) and type each line of the example yourself before running it.

{p 4 8 2}
3. Whenever you meet an unfamiliar command, type {cmd:help} followed by the command name.

{p 4 8 2}
4. Be persistent: 30 minutes a day and you will be a Stata beginner in one week.

{p 4 4 2}
{bf:Dingyuan Accounting} adheres to the principle of
{bf:scientific and standardized, humane and good} and hopes every beginner
learns with joy.

